## What shipped

`exportFormRecordPdf` (REC-7 "export ANY record") + approved-record sealing
(ACC-7), reusing the spec-40 Task 9 infrastructure exactly as designed (D-5:
one PDF pipeline, one retention discipline):

1. **Content plane** — `buildRecordContent` (forms.ts) reads record + template
   + sections + fields + values + clause-registry display rows in ONE tenant
   transaction (RLS), resolves every `title_key`/`label_key` from the SHARED
   `frontend/messages/{en,es,pt}.json` catalogs (bundle-time JSON import —
   BC-7 single source, no drift copy), and writes a `kind:'form_record'`
   content JSON to `tenants/<t>/records/<recordId>.json` (GeneralBucket).
   Locale = tenant `documentLocale` (same DDB META/ORG item getTenantSettings
   reads; graceful `en` default). Deterministic serialization → PdfRenderFn's
   body-sha cache: unchanged records never relaunch chromium.
2. **Render** — `template.ts` gains a `form_record` layout (meta block with
   Status/Opened/Completed/Approved rows + per-section label/value tables,
   required `*` markers, `—` for unfilled, everything HTML-escaped). Same
   brand shell as controlled documents; PdfRenderFn itself UNCHANGED (kind
   dispatch is inside buildDocumentHtml).
3. **Export** — `exportFormRecordPdf(recordId)`: build → upload JSON → invoke
   PdfRenderFn → presign the cached pdfKey GET 15 min (STO-4 parity). Typed
   errors: RECORD_NOT_FOUND / EXPORT_NOT_CONFIGURED / RENDER_FAILED.
4. **Seal on approve** — inside `approveFormRecord`'s txn AFTER the status
   flip (content re-read sees APPROVED + approver): retention policy
   `record_type='form_record'` (default 7y `review_before_disposal` seeded if
   absent — m1 pattern), render, CopyObject → EvidenceVault
   `tenants/<t>/sealed/records/<recordId>-<sha12>.pdf` with per-object
   `ObjectLockRetainUntilDate` (mode from env: GOVERNANCE dev / COMPLIANCE
   prod — BC-10, bucket default is safety net only), INSERT `m4.records`
   (retain_until == object_lock_until, `record_type='form_record'`,
   `source_module='M4'`, standard per BC-6 below) RETURNING id →
   `forms.records.m4_record_id` stamped in the SAME transaction (ACC-7).
   Seal failure → rollback → approval blocked (no approved-but-unsealed
   records). Unconfigured env (hermetic lane) skips honestly: audit payload
   `sealed:false, reason:'SEAL_NOT_CONFIGURED'`.
5. **BC-6 standard derivation** — seed `standards[]` carries `'IMS'` alongside
   concrete standards, so: strip `IMS`; exactly one concrete left → that
   standard; else `IMS` (m4.records CHECK widened in 011). Pinned both ways.
6. **Audit** — `FormRecord.Approved` payload now carries the seal record
   (`sealed`, `sealedKey`, `m4RecordId`, `retentionYears`, `lockMode`,
   `retainUntil`); no new detailTypes → no registry change needed.

