## Carry-forwards (named, non-blocking)

1. Non-`clause` relation values render as bare UUIDs in the PDF (clause
   relations dereference via the registry: "ISO9001 8.7 — Title"). Per-target
   display resolution (NC description, audit title, …) is a follow-up, not
   silently pretty-printed.
2. PDF chrome (table headers, "Controlled Document" stamp, meta row labels)
   is English by template convention (same as the spec-40 manual PDFs); field
   labels + booleans localize via tenant `documentLocale`. Localized chrome =
   owner call.
3. Re-approval after reopen seals a NEW content-addressed object
   (`<recordId>-<sha12>.pdf`) + new m4 row and repoints `m4_record_id`; the
   prior sealed object stays locked (by design — each approval is evidence).
4. Audit-event `standard` on FormRecord.* stays `tplStandards[0]` (Task 5/6
   convention) while the m4 row uses the BC-6 IMS derivation — the readback
   shows ISO9001 (event) vs IMS (m4 row). Consistency review candidate when
   the IMS enum reaches the event path (TODO-011 note already in forms.ts).

